course: dictionary
lesson: 7792
title: Context clues and a church name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Quaker is a member of a Christian group called the Religious Society of Friends. Here Quaker is a noun, a name for a person. The words around it give the clues. «Quakers, the Religious Society of Friends, worship mostly in silence and are known for peace-making and equality.» Worship, silence, peace and equality all tell you this is about a religious group.
explain: Look at this sentence: «More church families: Presbyterians, Pentecostals, and Quakers, who worship mostly in silence.» Quakers is in a list with other church families, so it must be a group of people. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A group of people, not a place or a thing.
explain: Quaker can also be an adjective, a word that describes something connected with Quakers. Look at «a Quaker meeting» and «a Quaker school». The word Quaker tells you which kind of meeting or school it is, just as the word wooden tells you what kind of table it is. Swap in your meaning, connected with Quakers, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A Quaker is a member of the Religious Society of Friends, a Christian group.
fact: Quakers worship in silence and believe in peace and simplicity.
fact: «Quaker» can be a noun, as in «Quakers worship mostly in silence», or an adjective, as in «a Quaker meeting».
fact: Quakers meet in a meeting house, sit in silence and speak when they feel moved.
fact: Quakers believe there is «that of God in everyone».
exercise: «Quakers, the Religious Society of Friends, worship mostly in silence.» What is a Quaker? | *A member of a Christian group that worships in silence | A kind of bird | A type of cake
exercise: In «a Quaker meeting», what does the word Quaker tell us? | The meeting is very loud | The meeting is for sports | *The meeting is connected with Quakers | The meeting is held on a boat
exercise: «Quakers worship mostly in silence.» Find and copy the word that tells us how Quakers worship. | worship | mostly | Quakers | *silence
test: «Quakers are known for peace-making and equality.» What do Quakers believe in? | Loud music and dancing | War and fighting | Great riches | *Peace and simplicity
test: Which phrase uses Quaker as an adjective? | Quakers worship in silence | *A Quaker school | The Quakers met today | Quaker is a church
exam: Which phrase shows Quaker used as an adjective? | *a Quaker meeting | the Quaker people are kind | Quakers are a Christian group | Quakers, who worship in silence
